      "sentence": "At Las Torres Patagonia, a historic ranch‑turned‑hotel within the park, 150 horses roam freely across 14,800 acres of land before being gathered at dawn for guest rides.",
      "explanation": "En español, el adjetivo compuesto se forma con guion para unir dos sustantivos que describen a otro sustantivo, indicando que el ranch se ha convertido en hotel."
    },
    {
      "grammar_point": "Non‑restrictive relative clause introduced by \"which\"",
      "sentence": "the experiences draw on the therapeutic power of spending time with horses, which has been shown to ease anxiety, improve emotional awareness and build self-esteem.",
      "explanation": "Esta cláusula relativa no restrictiva añade información adicional sobre \"the therapeutic power\"; en español suele traducirse con \"que\" o \"lo cual\" y va entre comas."
    }
  ]
}

