    {
      "grammar_point": "Conjunción correlativa \"whether...or...\"",
      "sentence": "They affect people’s ability to have resolution … to have an answer and closure, whether a positive one that they’d hoped for or a negative one,\" said Shira Levine...",
      "explanation": "Introduce una alternativa o opción entre dos posibilidades. En español se traduce como \"ya sea... o...\" o \"si... o...\"."
    },
    {
      "grammar_point": "Oración subordinada adjetiva no restrictiva introducida por \"who\"",
      "sentence": "said Shira Levine, a former judge at the San Francisco immigration court, who is now legal director for the Immigrant Institute of the Bay Area.",
      "explanation": "Proporciona información adicional sobre el sustantivo sin limitar su significado. Se separa con comas y se traduce como \"quien\" o \"que\" en español."
    }
  ]
}

